    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d466">

                <pb facs="0533" n="429" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg429"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4376: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Switzerland
                        (Wilson), at Geneva</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-24T13:00:00-05:00">February 24, 1932—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>21. Your 34, February 24, 10 a.m. I do not now anticipate in the near future the
                    action contemplated in my 19, February 20, 2 p.m.</p>
                <p>On the subject of the Nine-Power Treaty I have made public a letter to Senator
                    Borah, the text of which follows. It is sent to you for your information and
                    guidance and that of the delegation.<anchor n="96" xml:id="d466-f1"/> You should
                    make the full text available to the press. You may show it to Drummond for the
                    purpose you mentioned. Here follows the text:</p>
                <p>[Text of the letter to Senator Borah is quoted in telegram No. 50, February 24,
                    1932, 2 p.m., to the Consul General at Shanghai, printed in <ref
                        target="frus:frus1931-41v01/pg_83"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, Japan, 1931–1941, volume I, page 83</ref>.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d466-f1" n="96" xml:id="d466-f1-content">
                <p>To the General Disarmament Conference at Geneva.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
